{"name":"Post-Apocalyptic","title":"Post-Apocalyptic","revision":232500,"url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Post-Apocalyptic","retrieved":"2026-09-06","license":"CC BY-SA","licenseUrl":"https://www.fandom.com/licensing","language":"en","blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Post-Apocalyptic is a genre of fiction that emerged from the idea of what everyday life would be like if a society collapsed. The apocalytic event may be climatic, such as runaway climate change; natural, such as an impact event; man-made, such as nuclear holocausts; medical, such as a plague or virus, whether natural or man-made; or imaginary, such as a zombie apocalypse or an alien invasion. The story may involve attempts to prevent an apocalypse event, deal with the impact and consequences of the event itself, or may be Post-Apocalyptic, and be set after the event. The time frame may be immediately after the catastrophe, focusing on the travails or psychology of survivors, the way to maintain the human race alive and together as one, or considerably later, often including the theme that the existence of pre-catastrophe civilization has been forgotten (or mythologized). Post-apocalyptic stories often take place in a non-technological future world, or a world where only scattered elements of society and technology remain."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Other themes may be cybernetic revolt, divine judgment, dysgenics, ecological collapse, pandemic, resource depletion, supernatural phenomena, technological singularity, or some other general disaster."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Visuals"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Visuals in Post-Apocalyptic worlds can vary based on the timeline and cause of the disaster. Typically, most visuals may include:"},{"kind":"list","text":"Barren wastelands"},{"kind":"list","text":"Destroyed cities and homes"},{"kind":"list","text":"Deserted, looted stores"},{"kind":"list","text":"Modified, dirty vehicles"},{"kind":"list","text":"Weaponry, notably guns and blades"},{"kind":"list","text":"Little to no wildlife, or overwhelming abundance of wildlife"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Fashion"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Fashion in Post-Apocalyptic scenarios are based on what is needed for survival and what one can carry without too much effort. On the other hand, the aesthetic community focuses on how proper clothing can be styled. Fabrics can be light and breathable or heavy and warm depending on the season and the ability to have free movement is key. The most important element of Post-Apocalyptic fashion is protection from elements, especially if battle or inclimate weather is abundant."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Key items include:"},{"kind":"list","text":"Heavy boots such as New Rock Boots"},{"kind":"list","text":"Cargo pants"},{"kind":"list","text":"Long sleeves"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hoods"},{"kind":"list","text":"Dust/gas masks"},{"kind":"list","text":"Goggles"},{"kind":"list","text":"Loose fitting tops"},{"kind":"list","text":"Knee/Elbow pads"},{"kind":"list","text":"Scarves"},{"kind":"list","text":"Gloves"},{"kind":"list","text":"Ponchos"},{"kind":"list","text":"Heavy coats"},{"kind":"list","text":"Leather, cotton, spandex"},{"kind":"list","text":"Various clothing made from used rubber tyres etc"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Fashion items include:"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jean shorts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Crop tops"},{"kind":"list","text":"Vests"},{"kind":"list","text":"Harnesses"},{"kind":"list","text":"Belts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Tall socks"},{"kind":"list","text":"Makeshift armor"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bralettes"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Festivals"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Although Post-Apocalyptic is a fiction based aesthetic, it is seen in the real world through some festivals that are similar to Renaissance Faires. Attendees wear post-apocalyptic fashion and roleplay as if they are in an post-apocalyptic world. One notable festival is the Wasteland Weekend which takes place in the Mojave Desert."},{"kind":"heading","text":"Media"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Video Games"},{"kind":"list","text":"Half-Life (since Half-Life 2)"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Last of Us"},{"kind":"list","text":"Fallout"},{"kind":"list","text":"Telltale's The Walking Dead"},{"kind":"list","text":"Dying Light"},{"kind":"list","text":"Metro video game trilogy"},{"kind":"list","text":"S.T.A.L.K.E.R."},{"kind":"list","text":"Shadow the Hedgehog (2005)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sonic the Hedgehog (2006)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Wasteland series"},{"kind":"list","text":"NieR: Automata"},{"kind":"list","text":"60 Seconds!"},{"kind":"list","text":"Death Stranding"},{"kind":"list","text":"Sheltered"},{"kind":"list","text":"We Happy Few"},{"kind":"list","text":"Bastion"},{"kind":"list","text":"Horizon"},{"kind":"list","text":"Kirby and the Forgotten Land"},{"kind":"list","text":"Final Fantasy VI"},{"kind":"list","text":"Jak and Daxter"},{"kind":"list","text":"Most Shin Megami Tensei installments"},{"kind":"list","text":"Hyper Light Drifter"},{"kind":"list","text":"Stray"},{"kind":"list","text":"Chrono Trigger, mainly the year 2300 A.D."},{"kind":"list","text":"The Talos Principle"},{"kind":"list","text":"LISA series"},{"kind":"list","text":"Goddess of Victory: Nikke"},{"kind":"list","text":"Stellar Blade"},{"kind":"list","text":"Girls' Frontline"},{"kind":"list","text":"Arknights"},{"kind":"list","text":"Zenless Zone Zero"},{"kind":"list","text":"The Citadel"},{"kind":"list","text":"Command & Conquer Tiberium Universe (since Command & Conquer: Tiberian Sun)"},{"kind":"list","text":"Kemono Friends"},{"kind":"list","text":"Most Armored Core installments"},{"kind":"heading","text":"Tabletop Role-Playing Games"},{"kind":"list","text":"Apocalypse World"},{"kind":"list","text":"GURPS After the End"},{"kind":"list","text":"Deadlands"},{"kind":"list","text":"Rifts"},{"kind":"list","text":"Mutant Year: Zero"},{"kind":"list","text":"Numenera"},{"kind":"list","text":"JAGS Have-Not"},{"kind":"list","text":"War